From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: windows.storage: Buffer, InMemoryRandomAccessStream and DataWriter -- Telegram Desktop starts

Telegram Desktop's media controls construct a Windows.Storage.Streams
.DataWriter while the app starts. There was no windows.storage.dll, so
activation failed with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG, C++/WinRT threw, and Telegram
exited before its window, leaving only a crash dump.

A new windows.storage.dll provides:

 - Buffer (IBufferFactory; IBufferByteAccess for the bytes);
 - InMemoryRandomAccessStream: IRandomAccessStream, IInputStream (ReadAsync),
   IOutputStream (WriteAsync, FlushAsync), IClosable, clones sharing data;
 - DataWriter: default and IDataWriterFactory construction, every Write*
   in either byte order and the three encodings, MeasureString,
   StoreAsync/FlushAsync to its stream, DetachBuffer/DetachStream, Close;
 - RandomAccessStreamReference.CreateFromStream.

The operations work on memory, so their async operations are complete when
they are returned and call a Completed handler as soon as it is set.
include/windows.storage.streams.idl gains IInputStream and
InputStreamOptions.

Written from the documented API; interface layouts from Wine's IDL.
Gate: test/winrtstreams-gate.sh.
